  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Triples don't get flushed to the resource index immediately.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "There are occasions where this can impact RI-based policy evaluation.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Eg imagine a parent-child restriction policy that prevents parents being deleted before their children.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "There is a case where",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "content": [
        {
         "content": [
          {
           "text": "all children are deleted",
           "type": "text"
          }
         ],
         "type": "paragraph"
        }
       ],
       "type": "listItem"
      },
      {
       "content": [
        {
         "content": [
          {
           "text": "triples not yet flushed to RI",
           "type": "text"
          }
         ],
         "type": "paragraph"
        }
       ],
       "type": "listItem"
      },
      {
       "content": [
        {
         "content": [
          {
           "text": "therefore parent delete then fails",
           "type": "text"
          }
         ],
         "type": "paragraph"
        }
       ],
       "type": "listItem"
      }
     ],
     "type": "bulletList"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "There could be other situations also.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Suggest doing a flush as part of the RI-based resource attribute query.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "But, would this introduce a performance overhead?  Eg if policies are being evaluated when doing a mass ingest, it could cause a flush on every object.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Maybe instead an optional parameter on the attribute definition?  Or...",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    }
   ],
